// Part IV — Commands. Declared mode: reference.
page cmd_list {
  sites = [:manual]
  title = "config-weave list"

  chapter_header "config-weave list" {
    kicker       = "Commands · reference"
    reading_time = "2 min read"
    updated      = "2026-09-02"
    version      = "config-weave 0.1.0"
  }

  p <<'PROSE'
`list` prints the plays defined in a playbook, with their step counts and descriptions, followed by any playbook-local composites. It loads the playbook and reports load errors, but it does not run the full validation pipeline and never executes a script. With `--json` it prints the complete inventory instead: plays, composites and every package with its resources, gatherers, tests and scenarios.
PROSE

  h2 "Synopsis"

  code console {
    source = <<'SRC'
config-weave list [OPTIONS] <PLAYBOOK_DIR>
SRC
  }

  h2 "Arguments"

  table {
    rows:
      | "Argument" | "Meaning" |
      | "`PLAYBOOK_DIR`" | "The playbook directory." |
  }

  h2 "Options"

  p "All [global options](cmd_root) apply. `--json` changes the output as described below; the others have no effect."

  h2 "Examples"

  p "The human-readable form."

  code console {
    source = <<'SRC'
config-weave list ./my-playbook
my-playbook v0.1.0 — A starter playbook
  baseline  (3 steps) — Base configuration for every host
  web  (5 steps) — Web tier
composites:
  user_with_home  (2 steps) — A user and its home directory
SRC
  }

  p "The JSON inventory. Each package entry carries `name`, `description`, `builtin`, `resources` (with `concurrency` and `params`), `composites`, `gatherers`, `tests` (with `machine_kind`, `source` and `group`) and `scenarios`."

  code console {
    source = <<'SRC'
config-weave list ./my-playbook --json | jq '.packages[].tests[] | "\(.name) on \(.source)"'
SRC
  }

  h2 "Exit status"

  p "0 when the playbook loaded. 2 when it could not be parsed or failed a load-time check."
}
